VibeGuard for Orca — Attribution Notice
========================================

This project is a port and continuation of ideas, detection rules, and
engineering decisions from **DeepSec / VibeGuard** (VS Code extension +
Python core):

    https://github.com/Unclecheng-li/DeepSec

DeepSec is Copyright (c) 2026 VibeGuard contributors, released under the
MIT License (see LICENSE).

What was taken from DeepSec (see `docs/02-deepsec-fidelity.md` for the
full fidelity analysis):

- L1 rule set: secret regexes, sensitive-assignment + Shannon entropy
  analysis (thresholds 3.8/4.5), insecure-config and AI-pattern rules
  (`deepsec/shield/rules/patterns.py`)
- L2 SAST rules (`deepsec/shield/rules/sast.py`)
- L3 endpoint semantic checks (`deepsec/shield/rules/ai_audit.py`)
- Scan orchestration: skip lists, size limits, dedup semantics
  (`deepsec/shield/scanner.py`)
- The redaction-before-LLM principle and the audit JSON schema

What is different here:

- The Python core and Tree-sitter AST analysis were NOT ported. L2/L3
  semantic review is delegated to the agent CLI already installed on the
  user's machine (Claude / Codex / Gemini), with redaction applied first.
- The runtime is an Orca plugin (`pluginApi: 1`) instead of a VS Code
  extension.
